#### Article 19

1. Forms of services provided to women and children victims of violence include:  
a. health/medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of the victim's physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;  
b. medico-legal services which are a form of medical services for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;  
c. psychosocial services which are services provided by companions in order to recover the victim's traumatic condition, by providing a safe house to protect victims from various threats and intimidation;  
d. provision of moral/mental support to restore self-confidence, mental strength and independence in facing and resolving the problems befalling them;  
e. provision of legal services and assistance to help victims undergo legal processes related to the violence cases they face; and  
f. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.  
2. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Government;  
3. Provisions regarding procedures for services to women and children victims of violence shall be regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

#### Article 20

1. The Regional Government is obliged to provide complaint services by victims of violence;  
2. The Regional Government must establish a recovery house or safe house;  
3. Provisions regarding complaint services and social services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

## Part Two

Service Institutions

#### Article 21

1. Services to victims of violence shall be carried out by service institutions established by the Regional Government as well as non-governmental institutions;  
2. Provision of services by the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by regional apparatus having the principal tasks and functions of providing services in the fields of health and social welfare;  
3. Provision of services other than by regional apparatus as referred to in paragraph (2) may also be carried out by police agencies;  
4. Provision of services by non-governmental institutions as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by community organizations engaged in advocacy and services for women and children victims of violence.

#### Article 22

1. The Regional Government in providing protection services to women and children victims of violence through P2TP2A;  
2. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) functions as an integrated service center in providing protection to women and children from violence.

#### Article 23

1. Provision of services carried out by the Regional Government as well as non-governmental institutions includes receiving complaints and providing assistance;  
2. In carrying out its duties, non-governmental service institutions as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate and cooperate with P2TP2A established by the Regional Government.

#### Article 24

1. The Regional Government facilitates temporary protection, legal protection and support directly or channels to third parties, whether police, foundations, non-governmental organizations, or individuals for women and children victims of violence;  
2. Protection and support as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out from the time a report is received, either from the victim or other parties or from the time violence against women and children is known to have occurred.

#### Article 25

The Regional Government is obliged to facilitate the provision of legal assistance both inside and outside the court, to take legal action at the request of the victim.

#### Article 26

1. Medical services provided to victims include provision of visum et repertum, DNA examination, health examination, inpatient and outpatient care, as well as psychosocial and spiritual services;  
2. Services organized by P2TP2A must be carried out quickly in accordance with the needs of victims;  
3. Provision of medical services, counseling and reporting by P2TP2A shall be carried out free of charge.

#### Article 27

1. The Regional Government and or integrated service institutions for women and children victims of violence and community organizations, social organizations or non-governmental organizations are obliged to handle cases confidentially;  
2. Confidential handling of cases of women and children victims of violence shall be carried out at the request of the applicant, companion and/or counselor;  
3. Handling of cases of women and children victims of violence may be reported by the Regional Government and/or service institutions for women and children victims of violence, and community organizations, social organizations or non-governmental organizations if the victim and/or companion has given written permission.

#### Article 28

1. The Regional Government provides a safe house that is kept confidential with all its facilities, the financing of which is charged to the APBD;  
2. Services at the safe house are provided to victims by fulfilling the following requirements:  
a. filling out a form for personal identity and fulfillment of victim's needs;  
b. signing an agreement on the confidentiality of the safe house location; and  
c. complying with the provisions in the safe house.  
3. Services provided at the safe house include counseling, empowerment activities and victim independence;  
4. Service facilities at the safe house are also provided for child victims according to their needs;  
5. Further provisions regarding services at the safe house shall be stipulated in the Safe House Standard Operating Procedures.

#### Article 29

1. The Regional Government facilitates alternative housing that is kept confidential and needed by victims who are not accommodated in the safe house or victims who feel psychologically uncomfortable living in the safe house with all its facilities;  
2. The victim's alternative housing must be clear and can be monitored by the Regional Government and companions.

## Part Three

Service Mechanisms

#### Article 30

1. Integrated services for women and children victims of violence shall be carried out based on:  
a. the initiative of the Regional Government itself or technically by related SKPD either directly or indirectly; or  
b. at the request and complaint of the victim, applicant, companion, family, other persons, community organizations, social organizations or non-governmental organizations who know.  
2. Integrated services carried out by P2TP2A shall be carried out based on referrals from service institutions or based on complaints from victims or their families;  
3. Provisions regarding procedures and procedures for obtaining P2TP2A services in a Mayor Regulation.

# CHAPTER VIII

## REHABILITATION AND REINTEGRATION

#### Article 31

1. Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to obtain rehabilitation both physically and psychologically;  
2. Rehabilitation facilitation services include counseling services, medical psychology, legal assistance and skills training or alternative education;  
3. Every woman and child victim of violence who has recovered both physically and psychologically has the right to be integrated or returned to their family, community and educational institutions for those still in school status;  
4. Fulfillment of the integration rights of women and children victims of violence shall be carried out through cooperation and coordination among all related SKPD, vertical agencies in the region, community organizations, non-governmental organizations and family parties;  
5. Further provisions regarding the implementation of rehabilitation and reintegration shall be regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

